1104	// TestEmptyListReplacementKeepsRotationAndDropsHealth is the regression guard
1105	// for replacing a service's instance list with an empty one and later
1106	// re-adding the very same ids and addresses: the empty list must not delete
1107	// the service or its rotation position, and the re-added instances must not
1108	// recover the health observations recorded before the clear. The batch walks
1109	// the full lifecycle:
1110	//
1111	//   - a, b, c registered at revision 1; a and b observed healthy, c observed
1112	//     unhealthy with a reason, all at sequences above 1;
1113	//   - two successful selections return a then b, leaving the cursor on b;
